{#
  The lead illustration for a How to Play section.

  The artwork is a transparent PNG of the characters ONLY. Everything that
  sits above their heads is drawn here instead, over the top: the music notes
  for dance, the word cards for word. That split is deliberate.

  Words baked into a picture cannot be translated, so /es/ would show English
  cards, which is the bug in #199 all over again. Drawn here they come from
  the content JSON like every other string, and they are real text: selectable,
  indexable, and read out in the right language.

  The geometry lives in this file rather than in the content JSON because a
  character's position is a fact about the drawing, not about the language.
  `x` is the centre of that character's head as a percentage of the artboard
  width, measured off the alpha channel of the source art. Re-measure if the
  art is ever redrawn.

  Every board is the same WIDTH, and that is what keeps the characters the
  same size from game to game: the leads are laid out at one width on the page,
  so matching how much of the board a character takes up matches how big it
  looks. Height is free, and is whatever the drawing needs. Dance and word are
  rows of standing characters; draw is a scene around an easel and is simply a
  taller picture. Composition is done by scripts/build-howto-lead.mjs, which
  holds the scale each master needs and the reasoning behind it.

  Marks scale with the image via container query units, so the cards stay in
  proportion at 375px and at full width alike.

  "dance" and "dance-squad" share one drawing and differ only in the marks
  over it, which is the whole point of keeping them out of the picture. The
  impostor mode marks three players alike and one apart; Find Your Squad marks
  two and two. Same four characters either way.

  Draw carries no marks, and that is the same principle rather than an
  exception to it. Marks exist to hold words, and draw has none to hold: its
  secret is a drawing, which every language reads the same. The art already
  says who the impostor is, by the puzzled face, the question marks and a
  scribble that is not part of the frog. All three are shape, not colour, so
  it stays readable to a colour blind player without any help from the mark
  layer.
#}

{% set LEAD_BOARD_WIDTH = 1208 %}

{% set LEAD_ART = {
  "dance": {
    "src": "/imposter-dance-how-to-play.webp",
    "height": 429,
    "marks": [
      { "x": 13.4, "kind": "note-pair",   "tone": "crew" },
      { "x": 37.3, "kind": "note-pair",   "tone": "crew" },
      { "x": 58.9, "kind": "note-pair",   "tone": "crew" },
      { "x": 87.2, "kind": "note-single", "tone": "impostor" }
    ]
  },
  "dance-squad": {
    "src": "/imposter-dance-how-to-play.webp",
    "height": 429,
    "marks": [
      { "x": 13.4, "kind": "note-pair",   "tone": "squad-1" },
      { "x": 37.3, "kind": "note-pair",   "tone": "squad-1" },
      { "x": 58.9, "kind": "note-single", "tone": "squad-2" },
      { "x": 87.2, "kind": "note-single", "tone": "squad-2" }
    ]
  },
  "word": {
    "src": "/imposter-word-how-to-play.webp",
    "height": 429,
    "marks": [
      { "x": 16.7, "kind": "card", "tone": "crew" },
      { "x": 50.8, "kind": "card", "tone": "crew" },
      { "x": 84.0, "kind": "card", "tone": "impostor" }
    ]
  },
  "draw": {
    "src": "/imposter-draw-how-to-play.webp",
    "height": 665,
    "marks": []
  }
} %}

{% macro howtoLead(game, lead) %}
{% set art = LEAD_ART[game] %}
{% if art and lead %}
        <figure class="howto-lead">
          <img src="{{ art.src }}" width="{{ LEAD_BOARD_WIDTH }}" height="{{ art.height }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="{{ lead.alt }}">
{% for m in art.marks %}
{% if m.kind == "card" %}
          <span class="howto-lead-mark howto-lead-card tone-{{ m.tone }}" style="left:{{ m.x }}%">{{ lead.cards[loop.index0] }}</span>
{% else %}
          <span class="howto-lead-mark tone-{{ m.tone }}" style="left:{{ m.x }}%" aria-hidden="true">
{% if m.kind == "note-pair" %}
            <svg viewBox="0 0 64 70" fill="currentColor"><ellipse cx="13" cy="60" rx="12.5" ry="9.5" transform="rotate(-18 13 60)"/><ellipse cx="49" cy="52" rx="12.5" ry="9.5" transform="rotate(-18 49 52)"/><rect x="21" y="8" width="7" height="52" rx="3.5"/><rect x="57" y="0" width="7" height="52" rx="3.5"/><path d="M21 8L64 0V13L21 21Z"/></svg>
{% else %}
            <svg viewBox="0 0 48 70" fill="currentColor"><ellipse cx="13" cy="60" rx="12.5" ry="9.5" transform="rotate(-18 13 60)"/><rect x="21" y="6" width="7" height="54" rx="3.5"/><path d="M28 6C44 14 46.5 28 38 41C42.5 26.5 38 18.5 28 20.5Z"/></svg>
{% endif %}
          </span>
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
        </figure>
{% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
